# Line endings are load-bearing in this repo, not cosmetic.
#
# The frozen census files are md5-pinned, and those hashes are the audit trail for the blinded
# census assembly: they are asserted by concordance/build_suppl7_table1.py, recorded in
# concordance/BLIND_CENSUS_2026-08-31.md, and printed in the provenance block of every generated
# supplement. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) a checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, which
# changes those hashes — the directional census reads 76845dcc6131ab917717c7724da2c420 on Linux and
# f18e17dc5507008ee7b6e347e472d6b4 on Windows. A reviewer verifying the published hash by hand would
# get a mismatch and could reasonably conclude the frozen file had been altered.
#
# So: normalise text to LF everywhere, and mark every checksum-pinned or byte-compared data file
# -text, meaning git stores and restores it verbatim. Bytes on disk then equal bytes in the repo
# equal the published md5 on every platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Frozen, hashed, and byte-compared across environments — never translate these.
# Broad by design: the raw per-agent census files determine the pinned md5 of the assembled census,
# so a narrower pattern would leave the inputs to a hash outside the rule that protects the hash.
concordance/**/*.csv                -text
results/*.csv                       -text
results/blocking_summary.txt        -text

# Binary
*.pptx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
